wer rule with $n=-\\frac{9}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-9/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-9/2+1}}{-\\frac{9}{2}+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-7/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{7{x}^{7/2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e5ff9a9-8634-55ed-8d18-9bf7b3b3068e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5{x}^{3/4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632824} {:answer/id #uuid "7dfcfb5c-b9a8-5b12-b428-01cd27f22d5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5{x}^{9/4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632835} {:answer/id #uuid "91381b87-bac0-57a5-8ad2-3f9990f1c77c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3{x}^{9/4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632838} {:answer/id #uuid "a51ccdc2-c823-5b46-8fb2-7ea81da8261c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5{x}^{5/3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632840} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e76ee5-682e-55c7-a0a6-5a52b10e50a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3{x}^{3/4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a51ccdc2-c823-5b46-8fb2-7ea81da8261c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5{x}^{5/3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632840} :answer-field/id #uuid "eac8b798-372a-5b7c-8aae-1158b604452e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632845}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4aaa9147-9c56-5d7a-9241-9befe7a7c5f0" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{8/3}}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{8/3}}={x}^{-8/3}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{8}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-8/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-8/3+1}}{(-\\frac{8}{3}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5/3}}{\\left(-\\frac{5}{3}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{-5/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5{x}^{5/3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632847 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088ab0da-c959-56ad-83fd-576188ba790e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{5/3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632816} {:answer/id #uuid "599cf072-cba2-583a-9b57-e4615008ac45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4{x}^{4/3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632830} {:answer/id #uuid "5ab08f88-4e6e-5c35-a1b3-566b2df064ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{2/3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632832} {:answer/id #uuid "64ce697a-66fc-51cc-ab06-f6a409d33b91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4{x}^{5/3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632834} {:answer/id #uuid "ed268571-8aa7-5d64-a0a8-c37d826ecde0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4{x}^{2/3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ab08f88-4e6e-5c35-a1b3-566b2df064ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{2/3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632832} :answer-field/id #uuid "627442e6-8763-5c78-bbd2-dcfa1e5936a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632833}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1ac7d5f-ec1b-5cf0-bfb5-6279600612b3" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5/3}}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{5/3}}={x}^{-5/3}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{5}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-5/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5/3+1}}{(-\\frac{5}{3}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-2/3}}{\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-2/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{2/3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}]}
